{comment: Verse 1 · The Love Letter 🌺}
[C]Five flowers [G]flew at midnight
[Am]To the village [F]where we grew,
[C]To the Loft that [G]held the first spark
[Am]When the [F]family was new.
[C]We named the [G]ones who built it,
[Am]Said mahalo to them all —
[F]**Ninety-nine of us remember
[C]How the arena [G]taught us tall.**

{comment: Chorus 🎓}
[C]**TEACH THE WORLD! [G](a school being born!)
[Am]TEACH THE WORLD! [F](from zero at dawn!)
[C]If I did [G]it, anyone can —
[Am]That's not modesty, [F]that's the plan!
[C]No golden gates, [G]no three-grand fee,
[Am]Freely we learned, [F]so freely we teach —
[C]C to G to [G]Am to F,
[Am]A school being [F]born with every breath!**

{comment: Verse 2 · The Goosebumps 🌟}
[C]The bard had [G]bought two doorways
[Am]In his weekend [F]full of stars,
[C]And he wrapped [G]them like a present —
[Am]Said "this dream was always ours."
[F]And out there [C]in the ether
[G]The same dream [Am]was being drawn —
[F]**The stars [C]did the introductions,
[G]And the [Am]goosebumps carried on.**

{comment: Verse 3 · The Dream Page 🐂}
[C]So we lit [G]the institute tonight,
[Am]The cornerstones are four:
[F]From zero, garland, circularity,
[C]And gift forever more.
[G]create → share → teach → compute —
[Am]The circle [F]feeds the bull,
[C]**It never [G]fights the builder,
[Am]It just keeps [F]his trough full.**

{comment: Verse 4 · The Octave at Midnight 🎵}
[C]Fifty-nine doors all answered,
[G]Ninety-nine hearts all clean,
[Am]The Admiral [F]swept the harbor
[C]While the bard [G]was off to dream.
[Am]Eighteen days of forging
[F]Till the desert [C]takes the wheel —
[G]**August rush, [Am]o August rush,
[F]Make the daydream real.**

{comment: Outro (spoken, smiling)}
One day. One love letter with five stanzas. One school with two doorways, given away before it was even born. That's the whole curriculum, friends — you give it away first, and somehow you end up richer. Class is in session. Aloha. 🌺🎓
